From: bonsai-27b-fusion <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs(fusion): run the ctest gate, and prove the head_dim
 claim with perplexity

Two things this ledger said were missing or unproven.

ctest -R test-turbo had never run in this worktree because the HIP build dir is
configured with LLAMA_BUILD_TESTS=OFF. Built the two targets after a reconfigure
with tests ON (the rest of the suite, including dspark, is never touched) and it
passes 2/2. More useful than the pass: test-turbo-wht reports max_rel=2.38e-07 and
test-turbo-quant-cpu cosine=0.983230, identical to the llama.cpp fusion, so the
codec and the WHT op are correct on this base too and the head_dim 128 failure is
in the attention / KV-geometry layer.

The head_dim claim rested on identical generation output. Re-measured with the
metric that actually fails, on the promoted runtime, on SC117 (head_dim 256):

  f16 6.9921   q8_0 6.9397   turbo3 7.1292   turbo4 7.0756

turbo3 at head_dim 128 is 8038.79 and at head_dim 256 is 7.1292. That is the same
metric failing on one side and normal on the other, and it yields the first usable
quality number for these cache types: TurboQuant KV costs 1-2% perplexity.

Also ruled out three hypotheses for the head_dim 128 failure, each by measurement:
PrismML's KV mean-centering (opt-in, Q4_0-only, flag never passed), a missing
upstream FA fix (only 3 unrelated commits in the range), and the codec itself.
