+
+## 2026-09-19 (later): the ctest gate actually runs here now, and the head_dim lead narrows
+
+The ledger above recorded that `ctest -R test-turbo` had never been executed in
+this worktree, because the HIP build dir is configured with
+`LLAMA_BUILD_TESTS=OFF`. That gap is closed: after reconfiguring with tests ON the
+two turbo targets were built explicitly and the gate passes.
+
+```text
+ninja test-turbo-wht test-turbo-quant-cpu   -> OK
+ctest -R test-turbo                        -> 2/2 Passed, 1.19s
+  test-turbo-wht         max_rel=2.38e-07
+  test-turbo-quant-cpu   block=32 row_size=56 norm=6.373180 cosine=0.983230
+```
+
+**Both numbers are identical to the llama.cpp fusion's**, which is worth more than
+the pass itself: the WHT op and the turbo3/turbo4 codec are numerically correct on
+this base too. That brackets the head_dim 128 failure to the attention /
+KV-geometry layer and takes the codec off the suspect list.
+
+The rest of the suite is still never built, so `ctest` without `-R` is not
+meaningful here and PrismML's `test-dspark-forward.cpp` (needs `setenv`) remains
+the reason tests default to off.
+
+### Narrowing the head_dim 128 lead
+
+Three hypotheses eliminated, each by measurement rather than reasoning:
+
+* **PrismML's own KV mean-centering** (`7fb3d5b` per-channel K-cache
+  mean-centering, `36d1dee` hybrid models + calibration guard). This is the one
+  piece of fork-specific KV surgery in the tree, so it looked like the obvious
+  suspect for "q8_0 KV broken here but not upstream". It is opt-in via
+  `--kv-mean-center FNAME`, documented as scoped to `GGML_TYPE_Q4_0` only, and the
+  flag was never passed in any of the failing runs. Eliminated.
+* **An upstream fix this base predates.** Between the prism merge-base
+  (`5ea87ddad`) and `b11046` the FA vec file changed in only three commits
+  (`73a43d1f6` mid/mmf races, `8e93a9773` sparse-fa, `16378d93f` gfx1201 tuning),
+  none of them about head sizes or quantized KV. So a backport is not the fix.
+* **The codec / WHT op**, per the test values above.
+
+### Where it actually lives
+
+The project's own port map records that a 512-token prompt batch selects
+`BEST_FATTN_KERNEL_TILE` while single-token generation selects
+`BEST_FATTN_KERNEL_VEC`, and that the tile path converts TurboQuant K/V to f16
+through the `convert.cu` tables. So the perplexity runs exercise the **tile**
+kernel and the llama-cli check exercised the **vec** kernel — and both produce
+garbage at head_dim 128. This is not one kernel with one bug.
+
+That splits the remaining work in two, and they are different problems:
+
+1. **q8_0 KV at head_dim 128 works on the llama.cpp base and fails on this one.**
+   Since q8_0 has no TurboQuant code in it, the difference must come from
+   PrismML's own 93 commits. Bisect there, with q8_0 as a control that needs no
+   TurboQuant knowledge.
+2. **turbo3 KV at head_dim 128 fails on the llama.cpp base too**, where q8_0 is
+   fine, so that one is genuinely TurboQuant. Chase it through the tile kernel's
+   K/V dequantise path in `convert.cu`.
+
+Neither affects production: every model here that runs TurboQuant KV is
+head_dim 256.
+
+### The same metric, on the other head size
+
+The head_dim claim rested on generation output being identical on SC117. That is
+strong but indirect, so it was re-measured with the metric that fails: perplexity,
+same corpus and chunking, on the promoted b10335 runtime, on SC117
+(head_dim **256**).
+
+| KV | PPL | vs f16 |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| f16 | 6.9921 | — |
+| q8_0 | 6.9397 | −0.75% |
+| turbo3 | 7.1292 | +1.96% |
+| turbo4 | 7.0756 | +1.19% |
+
+All four sane and tightly clustered. turbo3 at head_dim 128 is 8038.79; turbo3 at
+head_dim 256 is 7.1292. That is the head_dim explanation demonstrated with the
+failing metric itself, in the configuration production runs.
+
+It is also the first usable quality number for these cache types: **TurboQuant KV
+costs 1-2% perplexity** against f16 on this model, which is the price of the
+context depth it buys. q8_0 KV comes in marginally *below* f16, i.e. inside noise.
+
+Records: `temp_clean_later/bench-results/sc117-kv-ppl`.
